                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "The **GEO Stack** is a five-layer framework for **Generative Engine Optimization (GEO)**\u2014improving how reliably AI search systems discover, understand, trust, and cite a brand\u2019s content.[2][4]\n\nIts layers are:\n\n1. **Retrieval Probability** \u2014 Make content discoverable and likely to be retrieved by AI crawlers.\n2. **Extractability** \u2014 Structure content so systems can parse and accurately reuse it, using clear answers, headings, lists, tables, and FAQs.\n3. **Entity Reinforcement** \u2014 Make the brand, people, products, and relationships consistently identifiable across websites and platforms.\n4. **Structural Authority** \u2014 Build trust through quality citations, backlinks, expertise signals, and consistent third-party validation.\n5. **System Memory** \u2014 Maintain freshness and repeated signals so AI systems continue recognizing and citing the content over time.[4][5]\n\nThe framework is intended to be applied **bottom-up**: if content cannot be retrieved or extracted, stronger authority signals will have limited effect.[2] Unlike traditional SEO, which primarily targets rankings in search results, the GEO Stack focuses on visibility and accurate representation within AI-generated answers.[6]",
